{
  "abstract": "A crystalline tempered distribution on a positive-dimensional Euclidean space is a finite sum of translated and modulated full-rank lattice Dirac combs with complex coefficients if and only if its support and spectrum each admit a polynomial count of degree equal to the dimension in one closed half-ball along divergent radii. The two unit normals and the two radius sequences may be chosen independently. The geometric result gives a single bound on the number of sites of a locally finite set in the measured half-space in every open unit ball, from its ordered patch-volume bound and its half-ball count. Distinct sites may be arbitrarily close.",
